# Build context for the root Dockerfile — an ALLOW-LIST (external review #9).
# Everything is excluded, then only the build inputs are let back in: the workspace
# manifests and lockfile, the three packages, the runner and the scripts, and the
# licence files. A deny-list let ./repos (the operator's checked-out repositories) and
# a root .env into the image; with an allow-list a file nobody named never enters it.
# `node scripts/docker-context-check.mjs` evaluates this file and fails on repos/,
# .env, *.sqlite, .gaffer/, .git/, node_modules/ or a missing build input (CI runs it).
*

# Workspace manifests + lockfile.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
# Sources the image builds and runs.
!packages
!runner
!scripts
# Licence notices shipped with the image.
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md

# Never, wherever it sits inside an allowed directory: dependencies and build output
# are produced inside the image; local state, databases and secrets stay on the host.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.gaffer
**/.crew
**/.git
**/repos
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
